# STM32CubeIDE build output (regenerated on every build)
Debug/
Release/

# Python bytecode cache
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# 4-mic capture outputs, loose legacy form (no --tag, overwritten each run)
capture.npy
mic0.wav
mic1.wav
mic2.wav
mic3.wav

# Legacy flat sweep outputs, superseded by captures/<session>/ below
angle*_capture.npy
angle*_trial*_capture.npy
angle*_trial*_mic*.wav
angle*_mic*.wav
validation_plot.png

# Session capture data. Audio is bulky and re-recordable, so the raw trials
# and the listening copies stay out of git, but notes.txt and README.md are
# tracked: they are the provenance of a session (room setup, wall distance,
# what the capture showed) and cannot be regenerated from the board.
mic_sims_files/captures/**/trial*.npy
mic_sims_files/captures/**/wav/
mic_sims_files/captures/**/*.wav

# Internal working notes, deliberately not published. CLAUDE.md holds the
# always-true hardware and config facts, HANDOFF.md the project history and
# open work. Both were removed from the remote on purpose; keeping them
# ignored means an absent-minded "git add ." cannot put them back.
CLAUDE.md
HANDOFF.md

# Internal tooling and working notes, deliberately not published. The hook
# in .claude/ guards the .ioc against accidental edits, CMSIS_DSP_SETUP.md
# records how CMSIS-DSP was vendored, and the supervisor update is a draft
# for one meeting. All are kept locally, none belong in the public repo.
.claude/
docs/CMSIS_DSP_SETUP.md
docs/supervisor-update-2026-07-22.md
